+// patch sets). The scroll view is put at the top for that estimate. When the real, taller title is
+// measured, the content's offset no longer matches the top; UIKit reads it as the content having been
+// scrolled and collapses the title for the whole transition, and the screen arrives with an inline title.
+//
+// So once the estimate is applied, pull the content down past the top, as a pull-down gesture would:
+// UIKit then measures the full large title, and we put the content back at the top it measured. Both
+// happen in layout passes before the transition draws its first frame.
